  "text": "Could your body's defense system hurt you? Your immune system normally helps fight infections. But in sepsis, that response can damage your own organ. Look at the lining of a tiny blood vessel. Inflammatory signals can make this barrier leaky. Fluid moves into surrounding tissue. At the same time, clotting can obstruct small vessels. That can disrupt blood flow, so organs struggle to get the oxygen they need. The infection, Matt. But part of the damage comes from the body's response to it sepsis is more complicated than an immune system simply being too strong Some defenses can also become supreme. It is a medical emergent early treatment matter protection depends on control not just force",
